From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ad5xrecon <ad5xrecon@localhost>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 15:15:00 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] ams: the AD5X's English texts name its unit IFS; Russian
 Auto-Refill reads Автозамена
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

English is the identity locale: the screen shows a source string as
written, and no pack is loaded for it. Patch 0028's edits to
ui_xml/translations/en.xml therefore never reached the screen, and the
English screen still said "AMS is busy", "uses AMS slots" and so on.

Where the AD5X IFS is the backend in use, these texts are now their own
strings that say IFS: the busy refusal of a load, unload or device action
("The IFS is busy", Kiln's wording for the IFS settings rows,
AmsSubscriptionBackend), the warning for an expected IFS that is missing
("IFS not detected", HardwareValidator), the two print start warnings for
bypass and toolhead filament (PrintStartContext::ad5x_ifs_in_use) and
the telemetry event line "IFS Active". Every other backend keeps
upstream's AMS text. The keys are in every translations/*.yml, with the
translation their AMS twins already had (patch 0030 worded those as IFS),
so no language falls back to English. "The IFS is busy" was only in
en.yml and ru.yml; the other languages now have it too, which also
translates the Tune IFS and Pre-feed rows' reason there.

"No AMS Detected" (an error without a message; the AD5X backend makes
none) and the "AMS" key (no source uses it) cannot show on the AD5X and
stay as they are.

Russian: four Auto-Refill texts still read «автопополнение»; they now use
«Автозамена», the word the AD5X's Auto-Refill switch (patch 0052),
Settings > Filament Auto-Refill and the wizard's auto-refill rows use.

Tests: the AD5X IFS busy refusal, both print start warnings and the
missing-IFS warning say IFS, other backends still say AMS, and every
catalog has the IFS keys, translated and without AMS.

Upstream: not applicable (AD5X OS specific)
